      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning begins by identifying key parameters from the tests: open-circuit test provides core loss Pc = 580 W, while short-circuit test at full-load current gives full-load copper loss Pcu_full = 1660 W.\n\nFor part (a), rated load at 0.80 power factor yields output power = 150 kVA × 0.80 = 120 kW; total losses = Pc + Pcu_full = 580 W + 1660 W = 2240 W; efficiency = 120000 / (120000 + 2240) = 120000 / 122240 ≈ 0.9817.\n\nFor part (b), half rated load at 0.60 power factor gives output power = 75 kVA × 0.60 = 45 kW; copper loss at half load = (0.5)² × 1660 W = 415 W; total losses = 580 W + 415 W = 995 W; efficiency = 45000 / (45000 + 995) = 45000 / 45995 ≈ 0.9784, matching option D.",
