    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The normalized power of the nth harmonic is proportional to \\(|V_n|^2 = 1/n^2\\).  \nThus, the ratio of second harmonic power to first harmonic power is \\((1/4)/(1/1) = 0.25\\).  \nThis holds whether considering single-sided or double-sided spectra.\n\n\\boxed{I}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe normalized power of a harmonic is determined by \\(|V_n|^2\\), as the total power is \\(S = \\sum |V_n|^2\\).  \nFrom \\(V_n = \\frac{1}{|n|} e^{-j \\arctan(n/2)}\\), the magnitude is \\(|V_n| = \\frac{1}{|n|}\\), so \\(|V_n|^2 = \\frac{1}{n^2}\\) for \\(n \\neq 0\\).  \nFor the second harmonic (\\(n=2\\)), \\(|V_2|^2 = 1/4\\); for the first harmonic (\\(n=1\\)), \\(|V_1|^2 = 1\\). The ratio is \\((1/4) / 1 = 0.25\\), which corresponds to option I.",
