    "global index": "MedMCQA_1194",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To assess outcome from labour, cost, time\n\nOptions: \nA. Cost benefit\nB. Cost Effectiveness\nC. Cost utility\nD. Risk Benefit\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**B. Cost Effectiveness**\n\nCost-effectiveness analysis assesses outcomes (e.g., from labor or interventions) relative to costs and often incorporates time as a factor in resource use or discounting. Other options like cost-benefit require monetized outcomes, cost-utility focuses on quality-adjusted measures, and risk-benefit emphasizes safety over cost/time. This fits best for evaluating labor outcomes alongside cost and time constraints.\n\n\\boxed{B}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning process starts by analyzing the question: \"To assess outcome from labour, cost, time,\" which involves evaluating outcomes—likely from labor or interventions—alongside costs and time factors, common in economic evaluations like health economics or project management.\n\nNext, the options are compared: Cost-benefit (A) requires monetizing outcomes, which is not specified; Cost-utility (C) focuses on quality-adjusted life years; Risk-benefit (D) addresses risks versus benefits without emphasizing cost or time; Cost-effectiveness (B) directly measures cost per unit of outcome in natural units, incorporating time as a resource or horizon.\n\nThus, Cost Effectiveness (B) is selected as the best match, as it aligns with assessing non-monetized outcomes from labor relative to costs and time, without the specific requirements of the other methods.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 87,
        "output_tokens": 248,
        "total_tokens": 1081
      },
      "provider": "azure",
