      "generated_answer": "**B**\n\nThe study demonstrates successful laparoscopic myomectomy in 505 patients with no exclusions based on myoma size, number, or location, removing 912 myomas (mean 1.85, up to multiple) with median operating time of 60 minutes and blood loss of 90 mL. Comparisons across size (<10 vs. ≥10 cm), number (≤4 vs. ≥5), and technique groups showed increased time/blood loss proportional to myoma weight/size, indicating feasibility without these as strict limits. Only one conversion occurred, supporting that these factors do not preclude the procedure for experienced surgeons.\n\n\\boxed{B}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe study's objective is to evaluate whether size, number, and location of myomas limit laparoscopic myomectomy, using a prospective observational design with no exclusion criteria based on these factors. Key results include successful removal of 912 myomas in 505 patients (mean 1.85 myomas, 36.4% with multiples; mean size 5.86 cm), with median operating time of 60 minutes and blood loss of 90 mL, alongside comparisons showing outcomes scaled proportionally to myoma characteristics. Minimal complications (e.g., one conversion) indicate these factors do not impose absolute limitations for experienced surgeons, directly supporting option B as the most likely correct answer.",
