      "generated_answer": "**C**\n\nThe study reports a low yield of 7% (95% CI 3-17%) for detecting unresectability via SL and 27% accuracy, with additional value from biopsies changing management in 17% of cases. While SL prevented unnecessary laparotomies in some patients, the modest results suggest it is not definitively useful or useless. Thus, \"maybe\" best reflects the equivocal findings.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
