      "generated_answer": "Based on the study results, fenofibrate showed significant improvements in several sleep apnea parameters: it reduced the percentage of time with oxygen saturation below 90% (from 9.0% to 3.5%), decreased obstructive apneas by 44%, and reduced non-cortical micro-awakenings per hour. While the apnea/hypopnea index (AHI) did not show significant improvement, the multiple positive outcomes in other meaningful sleep variables suggest fenofibrate may have a beneficial role. As this was an exploratory proof-of-concept study with some limitations, the evidence supports potential benefit but would require further investigation.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
