      "generated_answer": "William got upset at his sister Jane and the handyman Genesis because they treated him as a child rather than the serious, grown-up man he believed himself to be. Despite his romantic obsession with Lola and efforts to act mature, they continued to see him as immature and equal to themselves. This undermined his self-image and caused constant irritation.  \n\\boxed{\\text{They treated him like a child instead of taking his maturity seriously.}}",
