      "generated_answer": "**G**\n\nThe Denali Complex, found in Arctic eastern Beringia (Alaska/Yukon), is defined by wedge-shaped microblade cores, microblades, bifacial tools like knives, and burins. This matches the description precisely, unlike Nenana (D; lanceolate points, no microblades) or other European/North American complexes listed.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
