    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4515",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following indicates a primary context?\n\nOptions: \nA. the discovery of an artifact in a museum or private collection\nB. an archaeological site found underwater\nC. a site where artifacts have been intentionally buried for preservation\nD. all of the above\nE. a site where artifacts have been moved and rearranged by humans or natural forces\nF. the presence of artifacts in a location due to trade or migration\nG. all except D\nH. the existence of a cache or collection of artifacts found where they were left\nI. artifacts, ecofacts, and bone exposed on the ground surface by erosion\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**H**\n\nPrimary context in archaeology refers to artifacts found in their original depositional location without disturbance, which directly matches option H describing a cache or collection \"found where they were left.\" Options like A (museum), E (moved/rearranged), F (trade/migration without specifying undisturbed state), and I (erosion-exposed) indicate secondary context due to relocation or disturbance. While B and C can sometimes preserve primary context, H is the clearest and most definitive indicator among the options.\n\n\\boxed{H}\n\n## Explanation\n\nPrimary context in archaeology is defined as artifacts remaining in their original depositional position without post-depositional disturbance. Evaluating the options: A involves museum collections (secondary due to removal), B (underwater sites) and C (intentionally buried sites) may preserve primary context but are not definitive indicators, D is incorrect as it includes A, E and I describe disturbance (secondary), F explains deposition mechanisms without confirming lack of disturbance, and G is ambiguous. Option H explicitly states \"a cache or collection of artifacts found where they were left,\" directly aligning with the definition of primary context as undisturbed original placement.",
