      "generated_answer": "**F**\n\nPennsylvania was established as a proprietary colony when King Charles II granted William Penn a charter in 1681, entrusting him and his heirs with governance rights, as reflected in Penn's 1701 Charter of Privileges. This distinguishes it from royal colonies (governor appointed by the king, e.g., G), charter colonies granted to groups (e.g., D), or independent/self-governing ones (e.g., A, C). Options like E or H mischaracterize Penn's Quaker-influenced but proprietary rule.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
