    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Frederick Douglass was a formerly enslaved person who became one of the most prominent leaders and speakers in the fight to end slavery in the United States. The passage itself discusses slavery and opposition to it, reflecting his core work as an abolitionist. While the Second Great Awakening influenced many abolitionists, Douglass was most directly and prominently associated with the Abolitionist Movement itself.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
