    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The rising literacy rates in late Imperial Russia and the Soviet Union most significantly impacted groups that were historically underserved in education, particularly the rural peasantry, who had limited access to schooling before the Soviet reforms. The Soviet government prioritized mass literacy campaigns, especially in rural areas, to modernize society and support industrialization. Therefore, the rural peasantry would have benefited most from these efforts.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
