      "generated_answer": "**A**\n\nThe development of complex society at Caral, the oldest known civilization in the Americas, is primarily attributed to the construction of irrigation canals from the Supe River, which enabled agricultural surpluses (especially cotton for fishing nets and staple crops), supporting population growth and monumental architecture. Other options, such as trade, defense, or religious hierarchies, lack strong archaeological evidence as the initial driver, while features like pyramids or plazas were outcomes rather than causes.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
