    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4521",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\nClearly, no longer can a dictator count on East–West confrontation to stymie concerted United Nations action against aggression. A new partnership of nations has begun. And we stand today at a unique and extraordinary moment. The crisis in the Persian Gulf, as grave as it is, also offers a rare opportunity to move toward an historic period of cooperation. Out of these troubled times, our fifth objective—a new world order—can emerge; a new era, freer from the threat of terror, stronger in the pursuit of justice, and more secure in the quest for peace. An era in which the nations of the world, east and west, north and south, can prosper and live in harmony.\n—President George Herbert Walker Bush, Speech to a Joint Session of Congress, September 11, 1990\nPresident Bush's \"new world order\" most directly resembles which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. Woodrow Wilson's Fourteen Points\nB. The Truman Doctrine\nC. The Monroe Doctrine\nD. Theodore Roosevelt's \"Big Stick\"\nE. The Marshall Plan\nF. The Roosevelt Corollary\nG. The Domino Theory\nH. Containment policy toward the Soviet Union\nI. Richard Nixon's \"Peace with Honor\"\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**A**\n\nBush's \"new world order\" emphasizes multilateral UN cooperation against aggression, post-Cold War harmony among nations (east-west, north-south), and collective pursuit of justice and peace, directly mirroring Wilson's Fourteen Points' vision of self-determination, free trade, disarmament, and a League of Nations for global stability. Other options like the Truman Doctrine or Containment focus on anti-communist unilateralism, while Monroe/Roosevelt doctrines are hemispheric interventions, and Marshall Plan is economic aid.  \n\\boxed{A}",
