      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. The Populist Party sought to address the struggles of the working class and farmers and aimed for significant reforms that aligned closely with the goals of socialism, which was also focused on addressing economic inequalities and advocating for the rights of the marginalized. Both movements shared a common interest in undermining the influence of wealthy elites and advocating for substantial economic and social reforms.",
