      "generated_answer": "The excerpt describes the British government's efforts to raise revenue from the American colonies through taxation, specifically via the Sugar Act of 1764, to pay for defense and administration. This aligns most closely with increasing taxation to generate government revenue, much like increasing federal income tax rates after World War I to manage national expenses. \n\n\\boxed{J}",
