    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4559",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How did Aurignacian technology differ from Mousterian technology?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mousterian technology was focused on the production of scrapers.\nB. Aurignacian technology was primarily used for creating stone tools.\nC. Aurignacian technology was less advanced than Mousterian technology.\nD. Mousterian technology produced more usable blade surface.\nE. Aurignacian technology produced more usable blade surface.\nF. Mousterian technology produced less usable blade surface.\nG. Mousterian technology was mainly used for creating hand axes.\nH. Mousterian technology produced more projectile points.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**E**\n\nAurignacian technology, associated with the Upper Paleolithic, emphasized blade production, yielding tools with more usable cutting edge per unit of material compared to the flake-based Mousterian technology of the Middle Paleolithic. Mousterian tools focused more on scrapers and shorter flakes with less efficient blade surface. Other options misrepresent tool focuses, advancement timelines, or production specifics.\n\n\\boxed{E}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning process begins by identifying the key archaeological context: Mousterian technology (Middle Paleolithic, Neanderthal-associated) relied on the Levallois technique for producing flakes and scrapers, while Aurignacian technology (Upper Paleolithic, modern human-associated) introduced blade production, which provides a higher ratio of usable cutting edge to material weight. Each option is then evaluated against this distinction: A is accurate for Mousterian but does not highlight the difference; B applies to both; C reverses the technological progression; D and F contradict the blade efficiency advantage; G confuses Mousterian with earlier Acheulean hand axes; and H inaccurately attributes more projectile points to Mousterian. Option E directly captures the core difference, as Aurignacian blades produced more usable surface area, making it the most precise answer.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 175,
