      "generated_answer": "**F**\n\nThe letter explicitly notes that \"the waiting has been long,\" directly pointing to prolonged separation as the core strain on the marriage, a common hardship for medieval merchant families. The trader expresses hope to return home once he can do so successfully (\"I cannot come home with nothing\"), but offers divorce if she cannot endure further delay. Other options lack supporting evidence in the text.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
