      "generated_answer": "Aerial photography is the best method for identifying large-scale land modifications because it provides a broad, overhead view that can reveal patterns, earthworks, and landscape changes that are difficult or impossible to detect from ground level. Features like ancient roads, field systems, and large structures become visible through differences in vegetation, soil color, and shadow patterns when viewed from above. Other methods listed are better suited for detailed, localized investigations rather than identifying extensive landscape modifications.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
