      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}  \nThe excerpts emphasize humanity's inherent corruption and God's sovereign choice in offering salvation to some but not others, aligning with the doctrine of predestination. Calvin explicitly references God's \"purpose of eternal election\" and that salvation is granted according to God's will alone. This directly supports option G, which highlights the belief that salvation is predetermined and not universally accessible.",
