    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Federalist #15 by Alexander Hamilton expresses frustration with the weak Articles of Confederation, exemplified by foreign powers exploiting U.S. impotence, including Great Britain's refusal to evacuate forts in the Great Lakes region after the Revolutionary War (as linked to treaty violations in nearby Federalist papers like #22).  \nThis directly contributed to the sentiment of national humiliation and disunion.  \nOptions D and H are related but less central to the core examples of confederation defects.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
