    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**J**\n\nThe passage describes Dorgelès rushing excitedly to read the mobilization announcement, feeling exhilarated, and reporting to Clemenceau that \"Paris is singing,\" indicating enthusiasm rather than sorrow, fear, skepticism, or indifference. Options A–D and E–I describe negative reactions or extend beyond Paris, which the text does not support. Clemenceau's optimistic reply (\"It will be all right then\") reinforces the positive mood in Paris.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
