      "generated_answer": "J. a burden that should be willingly undertaken\n\nThe poem repeatedly exhorts readers to \"Take up the White Man's burden,\" framing imperialism as an onerous duty to civilize and aid \"half-devil and half-child\" peoples despite difficulties like exile, resistance, and likely ingratitude. This directly matches option J's emphasis on the mission as a burden to be willingly shouldered. Other options capture aspects (e.g., difficulty in F, civilization in A) but miss the poem's core call-to-action tone.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
