      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Reconstruction promised equal protection and civil rights for formerly enslaved people through constitutional amendments, including the Fourteenth Amendment. However, these promises were largely abandoned, leading to segregationist policies like \"separate but equal.\" The Brown v. Board of Education decision sought to fulfill those unfulfilled promises by ending legal segregation in public schools.",
