      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. The growth of corporate power and banking interests during this period created significant economic distress among farmers and rural populations, leading them to seek political reform through the Populist party. This reflects the central themes of the Populist movement, which emphasized addressing the grievances of the working and agrarian classes against powerful economic interests.",
